 {:db/id "q-78297" :question/id #uuid "1040f4bd-3d1a-5f7b-8b2b-4c581d4ad345" :question/math-academy-id "q-78297" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection across the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/b9/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78297/ma-source-field/49f0e2c8b85371ff7d8bc05cc344495f93a847174566653e44ab107faa419dc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
