 {:db/id "q-78302" :question/id #uuid "a51c70cd-319b-5de1-a71f-816af37c3370" :question/math-academy-id "q-78302" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78302/ma-source-field/36deeee1b3a459eaf2aaafc1e90069a4f4186a7ffa2826a2ab25e8fedbee127a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
